    {
      "number": 2,
      "phase": "improve",
      "parent": 0,
      "status": "kept",
      "reason": "better timing than round 0",
      "idea": "look-ahead head register: precompute next cycle's dout so the read multiplexer leaves the output path",
      "plan": "The worst path runs from the read pointer through the 16-to-1 read multiplexer to the dout port, which must also leave room for the output delay. I will compute the NEXT head-of-queue value one cycle early (from the next read pointer, or din when that slot is being written) and keep it in a register, so dout comes from a register instead of through the multiplexer. Because the original reset is asynchronous and shows mem[0] at once, dout shows mem[0] while reset is active.",
